  ],
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\subsequence:of{S ::= a(n_)}]\nDeclares: T ::= b(k_) is \\real.sequence\nwhen: S is \\real.sequence\nsatisfies:\n. exists: N ::= n(k_) is \\function:on{\\naturals}:to{\\naturals}\n  suchThat:\n  . forAll: k is \\natural\n    then:\n    . exists: j is \\natural\n      suchThat:\n      . j = n(k)\n      . b(k) = a(j)\n  . forAll: k, l is \\natural\n    where:\n    . k \\:natural.leq?:/ l\n    . k != l\n    then:\n    . exists: j, m is \\natural\n      suchThat:\n      . j = n(k)\n      . m = n(l)\n      . j \\:natural.leq?:/ m\n      . j != m\nDocumented:\n. called: \"subsequence of $S?$\"\n. description: \"A subsequence is obtained by composing the original sequence\n                with a strictly increasing map of natural-number indices.\"\nId: \"57868fa6-364f-4ecb-9c1a-9b45b53fff96\"",
